    "summary": "I built it: three full bases curve around one empty cell, and a full bay tray stands in that cell. The checks found no rule errors and no collisions between parts. The bases sit at (0,0), (1,0) and (2,-1), and the tray is at (1,-1). My first try spaced the bases evenly around the cell, with none touching another, and the configurator offered no place for a tray. Neighbouring bases have to touch. Following the house rules, I put solid end caps on the open faces (11 caps) and bolted the two joints between bases. That makes 15 parts, about 1284 g of filament and roughly 1840 minutes of printing. I added no props, since the brief doesn't say what the tray is for.",
